    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0671" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.5200 Compañia Terrenos Y Ganados San
                    Bodrigo/27: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Darniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-09T13:00:00-06:00">December 9, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>397. Your 287, December 7, 5 p.m. and 290, December 9, 11 a.m.<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d623-f1"/> I talked to Beteta yesterday and Carrigan to Mena today,
                    as it was <pb facs="0672" n="664" xml:id="pg664"/> not possible to see Beteta
                    today. Beteta wrote President about case last night according to Mena and it
                    will be necessary to await his decision. As prospects for cancellation are still
                    obscure and in view of time element, Carrigan asked Mena about 30 day extension.
                    Mena is taking this up with Beteta and stated it appeared “reasonable request”.
                    I shall see Beteta Monday on this.</p>
                <p>Regarding protection as cattle land I have left memorandum reciting quantity land
                    and cattle. This of course is contingent on final award regarding dotation since
                    such inaffectability is obtainable only upon formal request by owners and should
                    have been made before dotation.</p>
                <p>Carrigan pointed out to Mena that had company desired to make such request it
                    would have withheld its action pending reply from Foreign Office and since reply
                    was not received prior to dotation it had naturally not made this request. I
                    shall also bring this up on Monday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
